    "instruction":  "RF Front-End Chain Along a Straight Line\n\nThe file design.kicad_pcb contains a PCB with 8 RF chain components (U1=ANT, U2=LNA, U3=BPF, U4=MIX, U5=AMP, U6=LPF, U7=ADC, U8=DAQ) placed randomly. These components form a signal chain in the listed order.\n\nReposition all 8 components along a straight horizontal line in signal order and write the result as design.kicad_pcb.\n\nRequirements:\n1. All 8 components must be placed such that all their Y coordinates are within +/-0.5 mm of the mean Y of the group.\n2. X coordinates must be strictly increasing in signal order (U1 leftmost, U8 rightmost).\n3. Centre-to-centre spacing between adjacent components must be at least 6 mm.\n4. All rotation angles must be multiples of 90 deg.\n5. No component may be rotated exactly 180 deg (connector polarity preservation).\n6. No component may be added or removed.\n\nWrite /home/user/Desktop/answer.kicad_pcb.",
